# verification-misfile allowlist (T-2831)
#
# Signatures for task-file sections that legitimately carry command-shaped lines
# outside `## Verification`. One `<relpath>::<Section>` per line — the heading text
# WITHOUT its leading '##' (a '#' in the signature would be eaten by the trailing
# '# reason' comment rule). A trailing '# reason' is required by convention: the
# reason IS the justification, and "it's fine" is not one.
#
# Entries are still COUNTED and REPORTED as findings; they only stop the check
# firing. Removing a line re-fires that section. A NEW misfile anywhere fires
# immediately because it is not listed.
#
# Currently empty on purpose: the corpus of 2559 task files scans clean. The one
# real instance (T-2830, six commands under `## Evolution`) was REPAIRED, not
# acknowledged — an entry here is for a section that is correct as written, never
# for one whose commands should have been executed.
